#!/usr/bin/env bb

;; Novel Board runner (BOXP-246).
;;
;; Reads `Boards/Novel Board.md` in the Obsidian vault, treats the card lane as
;; the source of truth, and runs one writing agent per card. The lock, heartbeat,
;; stale-lock and planned-shutdown handling mirror the Task Board runner
;; (task-board/task_board_runner.bb) but use a separate state root so the two
;; runners never share locks.
;;
;; Routes:
;;   localllm      -> OpenAI-compatible chat completions on the in-cluster
;;                    llama-server (Gemma 4). The runner builds the context from
;;                    the management note and allowed vault references, saves
;;                    the manuscript itself, and never gives the model shell or
;;                    file access.
;;   claude-*      -> `claude --print` (same CLI contract as the Task Board).
;;   codex*        -> `codex exec` (same CLI contract as the Task Board).
;;
;; Illustrations are generated by the runner (not by the model) with the
;; generate-image skill and vault-local reference images, after the manuscript
;; has been validated. A missing illustration is reported as partial completion;
;; the runner never writes a link to an image that does not exist.
;;
;; Draft viewing (BOXP-247): once a manuscript reaches Review the runner copies
;; the private manuscript and illustration into a vault draft folder
;; (`Novels/Drafts/NOVEL-N/` or `NSFW/小説/草稿/NOVEL-N/`) so the human can read
;; them in Obsidian before approval. The copy is marked as unapproved, is
;; re-synced idempotently on every tick, never overwrites a draft the human has
;; edited by hand, and is separate from the one-time publication on Done.

(require '[babashka.fs :as fs]
         '[babashka.http-client :as http]
         '[babashka.process :as p]
         '[cheshire.core :as json]
         '[clojure.edn :as edn]
         '[clojure.java.io :as io]
         '[clojure.string :as str])

(import '[java.security MessageDigest]
        '[java.nio.file Files StandardCopyOption]
        '[java.time Instant ZoneId ZonedDateTime]
        '[java.time.format DateTimeFormatter])

